# Copy to `.env` for local dev, and set the same keys in the Vercel dashboard
# (Project ▸ Settings ▸ Environment Variables). Both are safe to expose publicly
# — that is why they carry the PUBLIC_ prefix.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form — Web3Forms (free, no backend). https://web3forms.com
# 1. Go to web3forms.com, enter the email address that should receive messages.
# 2. Copy the Access Key they email you and paste it below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Concerts — a published Google Sheet as CSV.
# 1. Make a Google Sheet with the columns from static/events-template.csv.
# 2. File ▸ Share ▸ Publish to web ▸ choose the sheet ▸ "Comma-separated values (.csv)".
# 3. Paste the generated URL here. Edits to the sheet then appear on the site
#    within a few minutes — no redeploy needed.
# If left blank, the site shows the sample data in src/lib/data/events.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_EVENTS_SHEET_CSV_URL=
